# TrichFree build configuration. Every value here is PUBLIC: it is compiled into the extension and the website.
# Never put a secret here (no service-role / secret key, no SMTP password, no database password).
#
# Copy to .env (or .env.production / .env.staging, used with `--mode staging`). Real environment variables
# override these files. All are optional: with nothing set you get a guest-only build (everything on the device).
# See DEPLOYMENT.md for which values to use in each environment.

# --- Backend (accounts, cross-device sync, optional pilot uploads) -------------------------------------------------
# Supabase → Project Settings → API. Use the publishable key (sb_publishable_…) or the legacy anon key.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=          # legacy name, used if the publishable key is not set

# --- Website <-> extension -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public website, https only, no trailing slash. The extension lets this origin (only) check its status, ask it
# to sync, open it or stop it; the website uses it for canonical/social URLs and the sitemap.
VITE_SITE_URL=
# Comma-separated extension IDs the website may talk to: the Chrome Web Store ID and/or a pinned pilot build ID.
VITE_EXTENSION_IDS=
# Pins the extension ID for unpacked (Load unpacked / zip) pilot builds: base64 DER public key. NEVER set it for a
# Chrome Web Store upload: the store assigns and manages its own key.
EXTENSION_PUBLIC_KEY=

# --- Website content (anything unset is hidden, never replaced by a placeholder) ------------------------------------
VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=
VITE_EXTENSION_STORE_URL=
VITE_EXTENSION_DOWNLOAD_URL=
# VITE_GITHUB_URL=                 # defaults to the project repository

# --- Research pilot (optional) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_EXIT_SURVEY_URL=
VITE_TEAM_EMAIL=

# --- Development and tests only --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_DEV_BRIDGE=true             # also let http://localhost and 127.0.0.1 message the extension. Never in releases.
